    "updated_at": "2020-11-19T12:56:29Z",
    "body": "There are a few things in this issue, so I'm not sure specifically which one we were holding it open for:\r\n* For snapshotting the `allowfullscreen` (and `allow`) attributes, we have WPT [here](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/iframe-allowfullscreen.html) and [here](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/iframe-allow.html).\r\n* For checking whether the document is active, there are fullscreen tests [here](https://wpt.fyi/results/fullscreen/api/element-request-fullscreen-active-document.html) and [here](https://wpt.fyi/results/fullscreen/api/document-fullscreen-enabled-active-document.html)\r\n* There is one Shadow DOM test for fullscreen [here](https://wpt.fyi/results/fullscreen/api/document-exit-fullscreen-nested-shadow-dom.html), but I'm not sure if it's testing the concern mentioned in the initial comment. I don't think we have any tests for `allow` that include Shadow DOM.\r\n* (And `allowusermedia` has been removed since this issue was last updated)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
